  "description": "<p>We wanted to set up Fedora and SSL, and ran with some issues. </p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p>After setting up SSL in Apache (80 redirection to 443, works as a proxy), and Tomcat using 8080, Fedora would return 404 errors on the GUI when browsing the repository. With CURL it worked well, but it doesnt translate (apparently) the URL to https.</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p>Details might be found on the next thread on slack: </p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://fedora-project.slack.com/archives/C0F71T4E9/p1616168449029000\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://fedora-project.slack.com/archives/C0F71T4E9/p1616168449029000</a></p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p> </p>",
